.TH A4\-KEYCODES 1 a4\-VERSION
.SH NAME
a4\-keycodes \- display key and mouse event codes for use in a4 configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B a4\-keycodes
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B a4\-keycodes
is an interactive utility that displays the key and mouse event codes
recognized by
.BR a4 .
It should be run in the underlying terminal and not from within
.B a4
itself. Press any key or use the mouse to see the corresponding code printed to
the screen. These codes are the exact strings used on the left-hand side of key
and mouse bindings in the
.B a4.ini
configuration file.
.P
To exit press
.BR Ctrl\-c .
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
Each event is displayed on its own line as
.BR "KEYCODE: " <code>
where
.I code
is the string to use in
.BR a4.ini .
.P
Keyboard codes use the following conventions:
.TP
.B C\-x
The Control modifier combined with key
.BR x ,
displayed as
.B ^X
in the
.B a4
status bar.
.TP
.B M\-x
The Alt (Meta) modifier combined with key
.BR x .
.TP
.B S\-x
The Shift modifier combined with key
.BR x .
.TP
.B Space
The space bar.
.TP
.B Hyphen
The hyphen/minus key.
.P
Mouse codes use the following conventions:
.TP
.BR press\- n
Button
.I n
pressed.
.TP
.BR release\- n
Button
.I n
released.
.TP
.BR drag\- n
Button
.I n
held while moving the mouse.
.TP
.B wheel\-up
Mouse wheel scrolled up.
.TP
.B wheel\-dn
Mouse wheel scrolled down.
.TP
.B wheel\-left
Mouse wheel scrolled left (tilt wheel or horizontal scroll gesture).
.TP
.B wheel\-right
Mouse wheel scrolled right.
.P
A second press of the same button at the same position within the
double-click interval (the
.B dbl_click_ms
setting in
.BR a4.ini ,
default 400ms;
.B a4\-keycodes
always uses 400ms) reports the
.B dbl\-
prefixed forms
.BR dbl\-press\- n ,
.BR dbl\-drag\- n ,
and
.BR dbl\-release\- n .
A third press within the interval reports the
.B tpl\-
prefixed forms, e.g.\&
.BR tpl\-press\- n .
.P
Modifier prefixes
.BR M\- ,
.BR C\- ,
and
.B S\-
may appear before mouse codes as well, e.g.\&
.BR C\-press\-1 .
.P
In
.B a4.ini
the shorthand
.BR click\- n
(also
.BR dbl\-click\- n
and
.BR tpl\-click\- n )
binds the press and release of button
.I n
as a pair;
.B a4\-keycodes
reports the individual
.BR press\- n
and
.BR release\- n
events that make it up.
.P
Note that button\-1 codes with no modifier, with
.BR C\- ,
or with
.B M\-C\-
(including their
.BR dbl\- / tpl\-
forms) are reserved by
.B a4
for text selection in terminal windows and cannot be bound in the
.B [MouseTermwinActions]
section.
.SH EXAMPLES
To find the code for Ctrl\-PageDown, run
.B a4\-keycodes
and press
.BR Ctrl\-PageDown .
The output might be:
.P
.B "    KEYCODE: C\-PageDown"
.P
This can then be used directly in
.B a4.ini
as:
.P
.B "    C\-PageDown = view _next"
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR a4 (1)
